// Title: VBA DLL Loaded Via Office Application
// ID: e6ce8457-68b1-485b-9bdd-3c2b5d679aa9
// Status: test
// Level: high
// Author: Antonlovesdnb
// Date: 2020-02-19
// Tags: attack.execution, attack.t1204.002
// Description: Detects VB DLL's loaded by an office application. Which could indicate the presence of VBA Macros.
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((src.process.image.path endswithCIS "\\excel.exe" OR src.process.image.path endswithCIS "\\mspub.exe" OR src.process.image.path endswithCIS "\\onenote.exe" OR src.process.image.path endswithCIS "\\onenoteim.exe" OR src.process.image.path endswithCIS "\\outlook.exe" OR src.process.image.path endswithCIS "\\powerpnt.exe" OR src.process.image.path endswithCIS "\\winword.exe") AND (ImageLoaded endswithCIS "\\VBE7.DLL" OR ImageLoaded endswithCIS "\\VBEUI.DLL" OR ImageLoaded endswithCIS "\\VBE7INTL.DLL"))
